  "description": "COMEN01C performs no dataset access whatsoever - it declares no SELECT and no FD, and its five EXEC CICS statements are one RETURN, two XCTL, one SEND MAP and one RECEIVE MAP, with no READ, STARTBR, READNEXT, WRITE, REWRITE or DELETE anywhere in its 282 lines. That absence is behaviour and it is asserted positively rather than by omission: the security file IS seeded, at the eighty bytes app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy declares, so it is present and readable throughout the run, and both record channels of the fingerprint must still come back completely empty. Seeding without expecting is the point - a case that merely omitted the dataset could not tell 'the unit read nothing' from 'nobody looked'. The rows are the in-stream data of app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl, whose literal password span is the legacy design's placeholder and is never read here.",
